  "description": "KATFOD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C61 H119 Co4 Gd3 N2 O32 P2. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.292-3.962 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.13-111.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C61H119Co4Gd3N2O32P2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Co(III), Gd(III).",
